-- Tests for ea-examination.l4 (Evidence Act 1893, ss 137 to 169).
-- Expected values are read off the Act's text and illustrations.  Generated by generators/ea_tests_3.py.

`s139 examination in chief` MEANS `Examination Facts` WITH
    `the examination is by the party who called the witness` IS TRUE
    `the examination is by the adverse party` IS FALSE
    `the examination is of a witness who was cross-examined and is then examined by the party who called the witness` IS FALSE
    `the examination relates to relevant facts` IS FALSE
    `the re-examination is directed to the explanation of matters referred to in cross-examination` IS FALSE
    `new matter is introduced in re-examination by permission of the court` IS FALSE
    `the question suggests the answer which the person putting it wishes or expects to receive, or suggests disputed facts as to which the witness is to testify` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party objects to the leading question` IS FALSE
    `the court permits the leading question` IS FALSE
    `the question is as to a matter which is introductory or undisputed, or which has in the court's opinion already been sufficiently proved` IS FALSE
    `the question puts into the mouth of the witness the very words which the witness is to echo back` IS FALSE
    `the question assumes that facts have been proved which have not been proved, or that particular answers have been given contrary to the fact` IS FALSE
    `the court has prohibited leading questions to a witness who shows a strong interest or bias in favour of the cross-examining party` IS FALSE

