`s147(1) a previous written statement, cross-examined without showing it` MEANS `Previous Statement Facts` WITH
    `the previous statement was made in writing or reduced into writing` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement was oral` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement is relevant to matters in question in the proceeding in which the witness is cross-examined` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement is inconsistent with the witness's present testimony` IS FALSE
    `the witness does not distinctly admit that the witness made the oral statement` IS FALSE
    `it is intended to contradict the witness by the writing` IS FALSE
    `the witness's attention was called, before the writing is proved, to the parts of it which are to be used for contradicting the witness` IS FALSE
    `the circumstances of the supposed oral statement, sufficient to designate the particular occasion, were mentioned to the witness and the witness was asked whether the witness made it` IS FALSE
    `the previous inconsistent or contradictory statement is proved by virtue of section 147` IS FALSE
    `direct oral evidence of the fact stated by the maker would be admissible` IS FALSE
    `the witness is cross-examined on a document used by the witness to refresh the witness's memory` IS FALSE
    `the document is received in evidence by virtue of section 147(4)` IS FALSE
    `a written law or rule of practice requires the evidence given by the maker of the statement to be corroborated or regulates the manner in which it is treated if uncorroborated` IS FALSE
    `the witness whom it is intended to corroborate has given testimony` IS FALSE
    `the former statement relates to the same fact` IS FALSE
    `the former statement was made at or about the time when the fact took place, or before an authority legally competent to investigate the fact` IS FALSE

`s147(1) a previous written statement, used to contradict, attention called` MEANS `Previous Statement Facts` WITH
    `the previous statement was made in writing or reduced into writing` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement was oral` IS FALSE
    `the previous statement is relevant to matters in question in the proceeding in which the witness is cross-examined` IS TRUE
    `the previous statement is inconsistent with the witness's present testimony` IS FALSE
    `the witness does not distinctly admit that the witness made the oral statement` IS FALSE
    `it is intended to contradict the witness by the writing` IS TRUE
    `the witness's attention was called, before the writing is proved, to the parts of it which are to be used for contradicting the witness` IS TRUE
    `the circumstances of the supposed oral statement, sufficient to designate the particular occasion, were mentioned to the witness and the witness was asked whether the witness made it` IS FALSE
    `the previous inconsistent or contradictory statement is proved by virtue of section 147` IS FALSE
