`s157(a) the adverse party calls evidence of unworthiness` MEANS `Impeachment and Corroboration Facts` WITH
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the adverse party` IS TRUE
    `the credit of the witness is impeached by the party who calls the witness with the consent of the court` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is of persons who testify that from their knowledge of the witness they believe the witness unworthy of credit` IS TRUE
    `the evidence is proof that the witness has been bribed, has accepted the offer of a bribe, or has received another corrupt inducement to give evidence` IS FALSE
    `the evidence is proof of former statements inconsistent with a part of the witness's evidence which is liable to be contradicted` IS FALSE
    `the witness gives evidence of a relevant fact and is questioned as to other circumstances observed at or near the time or place of that fact` IS FALSE
    `the court is of the opinion that those circumstances, if proved, would corroborate the testimony of the witness as to the relevant fact` IS FALSE
    `the proceedings are criminal proceedings and the corroborating evidence is the evidence of another witness` IS FALSE
    `a statement relevant under section 32 or 33 has been proved` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)` IS FALSE
    `the statement is admissible by virtue of section 32(1)(b)` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the maker of the statement` IS FALSE
    `the evidence to be corroborated was given by the person who originally supplied the information from which the statement was made` IS FALSE

