`s161(1) a contemporaneous note` MEANS `Refreshing Memory Facts` WITH
    `the writing was made by the witness at the time of the transaction, or so soon afterwards that the court considers it likely that the transaction was then fresh in the witness's memory` IS TRUE
    `the writing was made by another person and was read by the witness within that time` IS FALSE
    `the witness knew it to be correct when the witness read it` IS FALSE
    `the witness refers to a copy of the document with the permission of the court` IS FALSE
    `the court is satisfied that there is sufficient reason for the non-production of the original` IS FALSE
    `the witness is an expert referring to a professional treatise` IS FALSE
    `the witness has no specific recollection of the facts but is sure that the facts were correctly recorded in the document` IS FALSE
    `the adverse party requires the writing to be produced and shown` IS FALSE
    `the party called for a document that the party gave the other party notice to produce, and it was produced and inspected` IS FALSE
    `the party producing it requires the party who called for it to give it as evidence` IS FALSE
    `the document is relevant` IS FALSE
    `the party refused to produce a document that the party had notice to produce` IS FALSE
    `the other party consents or the court orders that the document be used` IS FALSE

